{
  "slug": "bci",
  "name": "Bci",
  "type": "plugin",
  "description": "The first BCI toolkit for researchers, developers, and security engineers. Threat modeling, vulnerability scoring, pattern detection, and neuroethics compliance for brain-computer interfaces. Reports are built with privacy by design and auto-redact PII. Please see Github README before use.",
  "longDescription": "Ships **8 skills**, **1 agent**, **2 commands** and **1 hook**.\n\n- **Skills** (8): `bci-anonymize` (This skill should be used when the user asks to \"anonymize BCI data\", \"anonymize EEG data\", \"sanitize neural…), `bci-compliance` (This skill should be used when the user asks for a \"BCI compliance report\", \"regulatory compliance check\", \"GDPR…), `bci-learn` (This skill should be used when the user asks to \"learn about BCI security\", \"what is neurosecurity\", \"teach…), `bci-scan` (This skill should be used when the user asks to \"scan for BCI security issues\", \"check my BCI…), `bci-threat-model` (This skill should be used when the user asks to \"threat model a BCI\", \"threat model a brain-computer…), `neuromodesty-check` (This skill should be used when the user asks to \"check neuromodesty\", \"review BCI claims\", \"check for overclaims\",…), `niss-score` (This skill should be used when the user asks about \"NISS scores\", \"neural impact scoring\", \"BCI severity scoring\",…), `tara-lookup` (This skill should be used when the user asks about \"BCI threats\", \"BCI attacks\", \"TARA techniques\", \"neural security…)\n- **Agents** (1): `threat-modeler` (Specialized agent for multi-step BCI threat modeling)\n- **Commands** (2): `bci-scan` (Scan BCI code or configs for security issues — run with --demo for a quick start), `bci` (BCI security toolkit — threat modeling, code scanning, and neuroethics compliance for brain-computer interfaces)\n- **Hooks** (1): `PostToolUse`\n\nInstalls with `claude plugin install bci@claude-community` from `qinnovates/bci-security`.",
  "compatibility": [
    "claude"
  ],
  "pluginType": "package",
